   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion to recommit with instructions Failed by recorded vote: 176 - 258 (Roll no. 227). (text: CR H3744)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8A000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "17:07:05",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question on the motion to recommit with instructions was ordered without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "16:51:45",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with ten minutes of debate on the motion to recommit with instructions. The instructions contained in the motion require the bill to promptly be reported back to the House with an amendment that adds a new section to provide the conditions under which withdrawal of normal trade relations with China can occur. Such conditions involve a situation in which China attacks, invades, or imposes a blockade on Taiwan.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36100",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "16:51:11",
   "committees": [
    {
     "name": "Ways and Means Committee",
     "systemCode": "hswm00",
     "url": "https://api.congress.gov/v3/committee/house/hswm00?format=json"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Bonior moved to recommit with instructions to Ways and Means and International Relations.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "16:50:57",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "16:15:31",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - The House continued with debate on H.R. 4444.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "12:09:23",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - Pursuant to H. Res. 510, the House proceeded with three hours of general debate on H.R. 4444.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "12:08:00",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H3662-3747; text of measure as introduced: CR H3662)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-24",
   "actionTime": "12:06:47",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 510 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "23:56:22",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 510 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 4444 with 3 hours of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit with or without instructions. Measure will be considered read. Bill is closed to amendments.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32700",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "19:02:15",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union rises leaving H.R. 4444 as unfinished business.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "16:37:46",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - Pursuant to a previous order of the House, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 2 hours of general debate on H.R. 4444.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32400",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "16:37:38",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable Ray LaHood to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32040",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "16:37:27",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House resolved into Committee of the Whole on the state of the Union pursuant to special order.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "16:37:17",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered by previous order. (consideration: CR H3596-3615)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30800",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "16:36:54",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Consideration initiated by previous order.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2000-05-23",
   "actionTime": "15:42:45",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "ORDER OF BUSINESS FOR H.R. 4444 - Mr. Dreier asked unanimous consent that it be in order at any time for the Speaker to declare the House resolved into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union as though pursuant to clause 2(b) of rule XVIII for consideration of H.R. 4444; that the first reading of the bill be dispensed with; that all points of order against consideration of the bill be waived; that general debate proceed for a period not to exceed 2 hours equally divided and controlled; that after general debate the Committee of the Whole rise without motion; and that no further consideration of the bill be in order except pursuant to a subsequent order of the House. Agreed to without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
